# Solubility of __MOLECULE__ in mixture __MIX_LABEL__ — BP-TZVPD-FINE.
# NOTE: Water is loaded as compound 2 (mole fraction 0 in xs) because force_qspr
# requires water in the compound list as its QSPR reference, regardless of
# whether water is in the actual solvent mixture. For mixtures that DO include
# water (e.g. water-ethanol), it appears twice as a compound — once at 0 (the
# QSPR aux) and once at the mixture fraction — and COSMOtherm handles this fine.
ctd=__CTD__ CDIR=__CT_PARAM_PATH__ LDIR=__CT_LICENSE_DIR__ # Global command line
FDIR=__FDIR__ nocompw wtln                                               # Global command line (UNIT default = kcal/mol, A^3, amu — matches pure-screen for unit consistency)
!! Solubility of __MOLECULE__ in mixture __MIX_LABEL__                   # Comment line
f="__MOLECULE__.cosmo" autoc                                             # Solute (compound 1)
f="h2o_c0.cosmo" autoc                                                   # Water reference (compound 2, QSPR aux)
f="__SOLVENT1___c0.cosmo" autoc                                          # Mixture solvent 1 (compound 3)
f="__SOLVENT2___c0.cosmo" autoc                                          # Mixture solvent 2 (compound 4)
tc=25.0 solub xs={0.0 0.0 __X_SOLVENT1__ __X_SOLVENT2__} force_qspr SLESOL xsolout_x_log10 wsolout_gg lsolout_moll_log10
# SLESOL: solve solid-liquid equilibrium (SLE) using DG_fus directly. Manual
# p.113: for high-DG_fus solid solutes the 'iterative' option collapses to
# log10(x_solub)=0 (the miscibility floor), and 'pr_ni' inherits the same
# clipped chemical potentials — both useless for ranking. SLESOL is the
# COSMOtherm-recommended alternative and produces finite log10(x_solub)
# values directly in the same output column.
# To revert to iterative: replace `SLESOL` with `iterative pr_ni`.
